+# Marginalia Books
+
+A website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop. It has four pages, linked by a shared header:
+
+- `index.html`: home
+- `books.html`: a catalogue of 12 titles with a genre filter (the selected genre is kept in `?genre=`, so filtered views can be bookmarked and back/forward work)
+- `events.html`: upcoming events
+- `visit.html`: opening hours, address, and a demo contact form with client-side validation
+
+The site is plain hand-written HTML, CSS and JavaScript. There is no build step, no framework and no npm dependency. It makes no requests to other hosts: no CDNs, web fonts or analytics. Text uses the system font stack.
+
+## Layout
+
+```
+index.html, books.html, events.html, visit.html
+css/style.css
+js/books.js     genre filter (books page)
+js/visit.js     contact form validation (visit page)
+tests/run.mjs   headless-browser checks
+```
+
+## Run the site
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8000
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:8000/. Any static file server works.
+
+## Run the tests
+
+The tests use Playwright, which must be resolvable by Node (for example, installed globally). They use Playwright's bundled Chromium if it is installed, otherwise `/usr/bin/google-chrome`. The tests start their own static server, so there is no need to run the one above first.
+
+```sh
+node tests/run.mjs          # all pages
+node tests/run.mjs books    # one page: home, books, events or visit
+```
+
+The script prints one line per check and exits with a non-zero status if any check fails.
